  "progression": [
    "The first year contains 60 EC compulsory. Practical Philosophy 1 precedes 2, and both precede Academic Writing. Theoretical Philosophy 1 precedes 2, and both precede Research Skills. The language diagnostic and tutoring are zero-credit requirements.",
    "Complete the first year for a positive study recommendation and progression. The 24 EC second-year core includes Philosophy of Science 1 before 2. One 18 EC Text, Context and Debate choice, 12 EC of specialisation and a 6 EC philosophy elective complete the year. A valid choice uses Quine in periods 1–3, Language and Cognition in period 4, and Art, Culture and Society and Philosophy of Gender, Race, and Intersectionality in period 5. The year-one theoretical courses meet Language and Cognition entry conditions.",
    "The year-three example uses Metaphysics in period 4 as the 6 EC thesis specialisation, followed by its thesis group in periods 5–6. The catalogue requires completion of year one, Text, Context and Debate and 12 EC of specialisation, plus prior attendance at the linked specialisation. Free choices are separately limited to at most 12 EC first-year courses. Future scheduling follows the applicable catalogue."
  ]
